WEBVTT


00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:07.500
Multicolor variegated or space dyed yarns,
whatever you call them, these yarns can be

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:13.560
challenging for those who are fussy about
the colors, pooling or flashing when

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:14.070
knitting.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:19.840
Pooling can be especially problematic for
machine knitters because the tension on

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.120
our machines doesn't change
while we're knitting a piece.

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:28.700
Hand knitters naturally very the tension
as they knit, so the pooling may not be as

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:29.420
noticeable.

00:00:31.365 --> 00:00:32.595
This worsted weight.

00:00:32.595 --> 00:00:34.995
Yarn has very short color repeats.

00:00:35.475 --> 00:00:38.385
The color changes every
six to eight inches.

00:00:39.675 --> 00:00:42.675
The swatch shows this pooling
in this particular yard.

00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:46.935
Can you see the diagonal line between the
purples on the left and the blues on the

00:00:46.935 --> 00:00:47.505
right?

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:57.180
Machine dyed yarns or space dyed are more
predictable because the color is laid down

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:58.920
in very specific lengths.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:04.560
Hand dyed yarns are not dyed with
precision, so pooling may be reduced.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.200
Now you can't just look at a cone or a
Hank of yarn and predict how the colors

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:10.830
will knit.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:13.110
You must swatch.

00:01:13.845 --> 00:01:18.375
And you need to swatch at different widths
to get an idea of how the knitting will

00:01:18.375 --> 00:01:20.895
look before you start your project.

00:01:21.345 --> 00:01:25.245
Think of how wide the back of
a sweater is versus the sleeve.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:30.779
Now you might like the look of this
patterning, and especially if you get a

00:01:30.779 --> 00:01:33.479
nice zigzag pattern on your knitting.

00:01:33.899 --> 00:01:38.970
But keep in mind that this is just a
swatch that measures about seven inches.

00:01:39.449 --> 00:01:43.380
The patterning would be very
different over a larger area.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:51.520
Here's some ways to
tame the color pooling.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:56.050
Try knitting every other row
with a different ball of yarn.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:01.000
Now, depending on the colorway, you
might also wind one of the balls from the

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:04.600
opposite end to reverse
the color sequence.

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:07.360
This mixes up your colors really nicely.

00:02:08.835 --> 00:02:11.805
For machine knitters,
try varying your tension.

00:02:12.075 --> 00:02:15.555
For example, knit two or three
rows at the main tension.

00:02:15.765 --> 00:02:19.905
Then switch to your main tension
minus one for a couple of rows.

00:02:20.174 --> 00:02:22.035
Go back to your main tension.

00:02:22.245 --> 00:02:27.315
Then switched to main tension plus one
for a couple of rows, alternating the

00:02:27.315 --> 00:02:28.215
tensions.

00:02:28.875 --> 00:02:33.734
Of course, you'll want to swatch using
this technique for accurate gauge, but it

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:36.484
can help mix up the colors and prevent

00:02:36.725 --> 00:02:37.415
pooling.

00:02:39.184 --> 00:02:40.445
Here's another idea.

00:02:40.924 --> 00:02:46.204
Choose one of the colors in the color way
and alternate the variegated with a solid,

00:02:47.225 --> 00:02:51.665
or use a contrasting color, maybe
black for the alternate color.

00:02:54.075 --> 00:02:58.515
What if you want the color arrangement of
a variegated yarn to be exactly the same

00:02:58.515 --> 00:03:03.045
on the sleeves that are narrow
as it is on the wider back piece.

00:03:04.575 --> 00:03:11.235
Use cut 'n sew you'll knit some
fabric, the width of your widest piece.

00:03:12.105 --> 00:03:15.345
Then cut out your Garment
pieces as if you were sewing.

00:03:17.115 --> 00:03:22.585
Now this takes some planning and it's
going to use a whole lot more yarn, but

00:03:22.585 --> 00:03:26.385
with this method, you could ensure that
both of the fronts had the same color

00:03:26.385 --> 00:03:27.765
patterning, for example,

00:03:29.795 --> 00:03:33.995
and the using this method, knitting fabric
for machine knitters is fast and easy.

00:03:35.865 --> 00:03:41.475
Don't let color pooling or flashing of
variegated yarns stop you from enjoying

00:03:41.475 --> 00:03:44.715
the beautiful variety
of this class of yarns.

00:03:46.595 --> 00:03:48.005
Thank you for watching.

